---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Weekly FX Brief"
  description="The PairPilotFX Weekly FX Brief: structured market context, relative strength, market structure, event risk, and scenario-based preparation for the week ahead."
  canonicalPath="/weekly/"
>
  <section class="weekly-hero">
    <div class="container weekly-hero-grid">
      <div class="weekly-copy">
        <div class="pill">Weekly market preparation</div>
        <p class="eyebrow">PairPilotFX Weekly FX Brief</p>
        <h1>Start the week with a clearer decision map.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          The Weekly FX Brief turns macro context, relative strength, market structure, liquidity,
          event risk, and confirmation requirements into a focused preparation plan for the week ahead.
        </p>

        <div class="button-row">
          <a
            class="button"
            href="https://pairpilotfx.substack.com/subscribe"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            data-analytics-event="weekly_brief_subscribe_click"
            data-analytics-placement="weekly_hero"
            data-analytics-outbound="substack"
            data-utm-campaign="weekly_brief"
          >
            Subscribe to the Weekly FX Brief <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
          <a
            class="button button-secondary"
            href="#inside"
            data-analytics-event="weekly_brief_learn_more_click"
            data-analytics-placement="weekly_hero"
          >
            See what is inside
          </a>
        </div>

        <p class="weekly-note">Structured preparation. Scenario-based analysis. No signals or guaranteed outcomes.</p>
      </div>

      <aside class="brief-preview card" aria-label="Weekly FX Brief structure">
        <div class="preview-bar">
          <span>PAIRPILOT / WEEKLY</span>
          <span>PREP</span>
        </div>
        <div class="preview-body">
          <div class="preview-row">
            <span>01</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Market themes</strong>
              <em>macro context + risk environment</em>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="preview-row">
            <span>02</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Currency watchlist</strong>
              <em>relative strength + weakness</em>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="preview-row">
            <span>03</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Pairs to watch</strong>
              <em>structure + decision areas</em>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="preview-row">
            <span>04</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Event risk</strong>
              <em>catalysts + volatility windows</em>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="preview-row">
            <span>05</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Selection framework</strong>
              <em>confirmation + invalidation</em>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="preview-result">
          <span>OBJECTIVE</span>
          <strong>KNOW WHAT DESERVES ATTENTION — AND WHAT DOES NOT.</strong>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container"><div class="rule"></div></div>

  <section class="section" id="inside">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Inside each brief</p>
          <h2>Built around the decisions that happen before an entry.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="muted">
          The purpose of the brief is not to produce more trade ideas. It is to narrow the market into a
          smaller set of conditions worth monitoring.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-3 contents-grid">
        <article class="card card-pad">
          <span class="card-index">01 / CONTEXT</span>
          <h3>Weekly Market Themes</h3>
          <p>
            The macro backdrop, central-bank considerations, broad risk tone, and the events most likely
            to affect the trading environment.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card-pad">
          <span class="card-index">02 / STRENGTH</span>
          <h3>Currency Watchlist</h3>
          <p>
            A relative-strength view of the currencies showing useful separation, mixed evidence, or little
            reason to prioritize them.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card-pad">
          <span class="card-index">03 / STRUCTURE</span>
          <h3>Pairs to Watch</h3>
          <p>
            Multi-timeframe structure and decision areas for the pairs that pass the earlier filters and
            deserve deeper chart work.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card-pad">
          <span class="card-index">04 / LIQUIDITY</span>
          <h3>Key Decision Areas</h3>
          <p>
            The levels and zones where a scenario becomes more relevant, including areas where liquidity,
            rejection, or displacement may matter.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card-pad">
          <span class="card-index">05 / CATALYSTS</span>
          <h3>News and Event Risk</h3>
          <p>
            Scheduled catalysts that can change volatility, invalidate an otherwise clean setup, or require
            patience before a scenario can be assessed.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card-pad">
          <span class="card-index">06 / EXECUTION</span>
          <h3>Confirmation and Risk</h3>
          <p>
            What still needs to happen before a scenario is actionable, along with the conditions that would
            weaken or invalidate the idea.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container decision-grid">
      <div class="decision-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">The weekly process</p>
        <h2>Filter first. Focus second. Prepare third.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          PairPilotFX applies the same sequence each week so market preparation stays consistent even when
          the market environment changes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="decision-flow card">
        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <strong>Context</strong>
          <em>What environment are we trading in?</em>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <strong>Strength</strong>
          <em>Where is meaningful currency separation?</em>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <strong>Structure</strong>
          <em>Which pairs have coherent multi-timeframe structure?</em>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <strong>Liquidity</strong>
          <em>Where does price enter a decision area?</em>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <strong>Confirmation</strong>
          <em>What evidence must appear before acting?</em>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <strong>Risk</strong>
          <em>What invalidates the scenario?</em>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container fit card">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who it is for</p>
        <h2>A research brief for traders who want a repeatable preparation process.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fit-list">
        <p><span>✓</span> You want a smaller, more focused watchlist instead of scanning everything.</p>
        <p><span>✓</span> You use market structure and price action but want stronger top-down context.</p>
        <p><span>✓</span> You want scenarios, catalysts, confirmation, and invalidation made explicit.</p>
        <p><span>—</span> You are looking for trade signals, guaranteed setups, or automatic execution.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container conversion card">
      <div class="conversion-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">PairPilotFX Weekly FX Brief</p>
        <h2>Make the first decision of the week what deserves your attention.</h2>
        <p>
          Subscribe through Substack to receive PairPilotFX's structured market preparation and follow the
          same framework as conditions develop.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="conversion-action">
        <a
          class="button"
          href="https://pairpilotfx.substack.com/subscribe"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          data-analytics-event="weekly_brief_subscribe_click"
          data-analytics-placement="weekly_closing"
          data-analytics-outbound="substack"
          data-utm-campaign="weekly_brief"
        >Subscribe on Substack →</a>
        <a
          class="text-link"
          href="https://pairpilotfx.substack.com/"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          data-analytics-event="substack_click"
          data-analytics-placement="weekly_sample"
          data-analytics-outbound="substack"
          data-utm-campaign="weekly_brief"
        >Read the existing research first</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container disclaimer">
    <strong>Risk note</strong>
    <p>
      PairPilotFX provides educational market commentary and decision-support content. It does not provide
      individualized investment advice, guaranteed outcomes, trade signals, or autonomous trade execution.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .weekly-hero { padding: 108px 0 86px; overflow: hidden; }
  .weekly-hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(380px, .95fr);
    gap: 64px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .weekly-copy { display: grid; gap: 24px; }
  .weekly-copy .eyebrow { margin: 8px 0 -10px; }
  .weekly-copy h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.8rem); }
  .weekly-note { color: #7f96ae; font-size: .84rem; }

  .brief-preview { overflow: hidden; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .preview-bar {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 18px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: #7f96ae;
    font-size: .68rem;
    font-weight: 850;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.025);
  }
  .preview-bar span:last-child { color: var(--accent-strong); }
  .preview-body { display: grid; }
  .preview-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 40px 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);
  }
  .preview-row > span {
    color: #5d7893;
    font: 750 .72rem/1.3 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }
  .preview-row div { display: grid; gap: 5px; }
  .preview-row strong { font-size: .91rem; }
  .preview-row em {
    color: #86a1bb;
    font: normal .76rem/1.4 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }
  .preview-result {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 24px 20px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(88,166,255,.08), rgba(88,166,255,.02));
  }
  .preview-result span { color: #668199; font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: .12em; }
  .preview-result strong {
    color: #c6e4ff;
    font: 800 .85rem/1.5 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr .8fr;
    gap: 52px;
    align-items: end;
    margin-bottom: 34px;
  }
  .section-heading .muted { max-width: 440px; justify-self: end; }
  .contents-grid article { display: grid; gap: 15px; min-height: 250px; }
  .contents-grid article p { color: var(--muted); }
  .card-index { color: #668199; font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: .13em; }

  .decision-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr;
    gap: 54px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .decision-copy { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .decision-flow { overflow: hidden; }
  .decision-flow > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 42px 150px 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 19px 22px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);
  }
  .decision-flow > div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .decision-flow span {
    color: #5f7a95;
    font: 750 .72rem/1 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }
  .decision-flow strong { color: #f1f7ff; }
  .decision-flow em { color: var(--muted); font-style: normal; font-size: .84rem; }

  .fit {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 54px;
    padding: clamp(30px, 5vw, 56px);
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 90% 0%, rgba(88,166,255,.12), transparent 25rem),
      linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(18,38,61,.95), rgba(8,21,37,.95));
  }
  .fit h2 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem); }
  .fit-list { display: grid; gap: 16px; align-content: center; }
  .fit-list p { color: #bdd0e2; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 24px 1fr; gap: 8px; }
  .fit-list span { color: var(--accent-strong); font-weight: 850; }

  .conversion {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr .85fr;
    gap: 50px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: clamp(30px, 5vw, 58px);
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }
  .conversion-copy { display: grid; gap: 17px; }
  .conversion-copy p:last-child { color: var(--muted-strong); max-width: 720px; }
  .conversion-action { display: grid; justify-items: start; gap: 15px; }
  .text-link { color: var(--accent-strong); text-decoration: none; font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .text-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .disclaimer {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: 20px;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
    color: #7890a8;
    font-size: .78rem;
  }
  .disclaimer strong { color: #9ab1c7; white-space: nowrap; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .weekly-hero { padding-top: 78px; }
    .weekly-hero-grid,
    .section-heading,
    .decision-grid,
    .fit,
    .conversion {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .section-heading .muted { justify-self: start; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .decision-flow > div {
      grid-template-columns: 30px 1fr;
    }
    .decision-flow em { grid-column: 2; }
    .disclaimer { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 7px; }
  }
</style>
